# Build context for every image in `infra/docker/` is `apps/`, not the repo
# root — which is the point. The desktop tree (`src/`, `src-tauri/`) is not
# reachable from here at all, so no image can accidentally COPY it and no
# `npm ci` inside a build can resolve against the desktop app's node_modules
# (plan §0, §7.1).
#
# Everything below is excluded because it is either reproduced by the build
# (node_modules, dist) or a secret that must never be baked into a layer.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Real credentials. `.env.example` is deliberately not excluded — it is the
# template, and having it in the image is harmless and occasionally useful.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Tests and lint config are not needed at runtime. They stay out of the
# context so a change to them does not invalidate the install layer.
api/test
**/eslint.config.js
**/vitest.config.ts
**/tsconfig.test.json

**/.DS_Store
